ng this afternoon, overnight and redeveloping tomorrow.\nPeriods of heavy rainfall will increase the threat of flooding\nand flash flooding .\n- This includes the following rivers...\nAnimas River, La Plata, Los Pinos, and Vallecito Creek.\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nDurango, Bayfield, Ignacio, La Plata, Falfa, Oxford, Bondad,\nHesperus, Breen, Vallecito, Mayday, Kline, Marvel, Tiffany,\nAllison and Redmesa.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-10-24T15:45:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Archuleta, CO; Hinsdale, CO; La Plata, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.e90202f1f6afd1fe91fe5187ef58da7e89d0b07d.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.e90202f1f6afd1fe91fe5187ef58da7e89d0b07d.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Watch","headline":"Flood Watch issued October 23 at 11:59AM MDT until October 25 at 12:00PM MDT by NWS Grand Junction CO","description":"* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues to be\npossible.\n\n* WHERE...Portions of southwest Colorado, including the following\nareas, Animas River Basin, Four Corners/Upper Dolores River, San\nJuan River Basin and Southwest San Juan Mountains and Utah,\nincluding the following areas, Arches/Grand Flat,\nCanyonlands/Natural Bridges, La Sal and Abajo Mountains and\nSoutheast Utah.\n\n* WHEN...Through Sunday morning.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, recent burn scars and other low-lying and\nflood-prone locations. Low-water crossings may be flooded. Storm\ndrains and ditches may become clogged with debris.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Flooding is imminent or ongoing with additional rounds of showers\nand thunderstorms expected through Saturday afternoon. Rivers and\ncreeks may still experience high waters even after rainfall has\nended.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-10-25T12:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Uncompahgre Plateau/Dallas Divide; Northwestern San Juan Mountains; Southwest San Juan Mountains; Paradox Valley/Lower Dolores River; Four Corners/Upper Dolores River; Animas River Basin; San Juan River Basin; Southeast Utah; Arches/Grand Flat; La Sal and Abajo Mountains; Canyonlands/Natural Bridges","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.a28b19253bb7550e7a42b701dae47ec9af4c8ee0.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.a28b19253bb7550e7a42b701dae47ec9af4c8ee0.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Warning","headline":"Flood Warning issued October 22 at 9:56PM MDT until October 23 at 10:00PM MDT by NWS Grand Junction CO","description":"* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall across the area is\noccurring.\n\n* WHERE...South Central La Plata County in southwestern Colorado...\n\n* WHEN...Until 1000 PM MDT Friday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Flooding of rivers, creeks, streams, and other low-lying\nand flood-prone locations is imminent or occurring.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 948 PM MDT, Gauge reports the La Plata River has risen above\nflood stage due to heavy rain. Flooding is ongoing or expected to\nbegin shortly in the warned area. Between 1.5 and 2.5 inches of\nrain have fallen across the area over the past two days.\n- This includes the La Plata River and the surrounding low areas\nnear the river.\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nHesperus.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-10-23T22:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"La Plata, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.50d9d55c23b1232fd65ae6fe78b20c1a59055270.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.50d9d55c23b1232fd65ae6fe78b20c1a59055270.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-10-23T23:22:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KGJT 232322 AFDGJT Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Grand Junction CO 522 PM MDT Fri Oct 23 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Flooding is ongoing across portions of southeast Utah and southwest Colorado, and is expected to continue through Saturday. - M